<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{{ m.company.name }} multi-year accounting review</title>
{% include "_styles.html.j2" %}
</head>
<body>
<div class="toolbar"><button type="button" onclick="(function(){var r=document.documentElement;var d=r.getAttribute('data-theme')==='dark'||(r.getAttribute('data-theme')===null&&matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches);r.setAttribute('data-theme',d?'light':'dark');})()">Theme</button></div>
<main>
<header>
  <div class="sub">Multi-year accounting review · {{ m.period }} ({{ m.years }} fiscal years, ended {{ m.first_end }} to {{ m.last_end }}) · based on filings available on {{ m.as_of }}</div>
  <h1>{{ m.company.name }}{% if m.company.ticker %} ({{ m.company.ticker }}){% endif %}</h1>
  <div class="muted">Industry: {{ m.company.sic_description or 'not stated' }} · Auditor: {{ m.company.auditor or 'not identified' }} · Prepared {{ m.generated }}</div>
  <p class="muted">Company type: <strong>{{ m.profile.label }}</strong> · amounts in {{ m.currency }}{% if m.profile.excluded %} · {{ m.profile.excluded }} tests do not apply to this type of company{% endif %}</p>
  <p class="muted"><strong>Caveats:</strong> {% if m.company.warnings %}{{ m.company.warnings|join(' ') }}{% else %}{{ m.none_text }}{% endif %}</p>
  <nav class="toc" aria-label="Sections"><a href="#summary">Summary</a><a href="#dashboard">Overview</a><a href="#findings">Suspicious anomalies</a>{% if m.set_aside %}<a href="#setaside">Set aside</a>{% endif %}<a href="#tests">All tests</a><a href="#text">Disclosure changes</a><a href="#method">How this review works</a><a href="#glossary">Glossary</a></nav>
</header>

<section id="summary">
<h2>Summary</h2>
<div class="card hero">
  <div>
    <div class="muted">Risk index for the period (0-100)</div>
    <div class="index">{{ "%.0f"|format(m.risk.index) }}</div>
    <div class="band {{ m.risk.band }}"><i></i>{{ m.risk.band }}</div>
    <div class="scale" aria-hidden="true">{% for b in [25,50,75,100] %}<span class="{{ 'on' if m.risk.index >= b - 25 else '' }}"></span>{% endfor %}</div>
    <div class="muted">Low below 25 · Elevated below 50 · High below 75 · Severe 75 and above</div>
  </div>
  <div>
    <p class="lead"><strong>Matters worth following up ({{ m.findings|length }})</strong>, most important first:</p>
    {% if m.top_sentences %}<ol class="tight">{% for s in m.top_sentences %}<li>{{ s }}</li>{% endfor %}</ol>{% else %}<ul class="tight"><li>None. No test found a warning sign strong enough to report in any year; every result is listed under <a href="#tests">All tests</a>.</li></ul>{% endif %}
    <p class="muted"><strong>AI investigation:</strong> {% if m.investigated %}the top {{ m.investigated }} anomalies were investigated across all the years they appeared in.{% else %}not run.{% endif %}
      <strong>Independent re-check:</strong> {% if m.findings %}every anomaly was re-checked against the original filings: {{ m.audit_summary.verified }} confirmed, {{ m.audit_summary.corrected }} confirmed after corrections, {{ m.audit_summary.unverified }} could not be fully confirmed and count for half.{% else %}not needed, because there are no anomalies.{% endif %}</p>
    <p><strong>The question that would most change this conclusion:</strong> {{ m.key_question }}</p>
    <p class="muted">Each year is scored on its own; the period index is the average of the yearly indices, raised halfway towards the worst year, so a single bad year is neither hidden nor allowed to define the period. It is a screening score, not the probability that anything is wrong.</p>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="card">{% if m.charts.risk %}{{ m.charts.risk|safe }}{% endif %}
<div class="tablewrap"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Fiscal year</th><th>Year ended</th><th class="num">Risk index</th><th>Band</th><th class="num">Tests flagged</th><th>Strongest finding</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>{% for y in m.yearly %}<tr><td>{{ m.periods[loop.index0] }}</td><td>{{ y.period_end }}</td><td class="num">{{ "%.0f"|format(y.risk_index) }}</td><td><span class="band {{ y.band }}"><i></i>{{ y.band }}</span></td><td class="num">{{ y.flagged }}</td><td>{{ y.top }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
</table></div></div>
<div class="card tablewrap"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Key figures (as first reported each year)</th>{% for p in m.periods %}<th class="num">{{ p }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr></thead>
  <tbody>{% for k in m.key_numbers %}<tr><td>{{ k.label }}</td>{% for v in k["values"] %}<td class="num">{{ v }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
</table></div>
<p class="disclaimer">{{ m.disclaimer }}</p>
</section>

<section id="dashboard">
<h2>Overview</h2>
<div class="card tablewrap">
  <h3>Warning-sign strength by accounting area and year</h3>
  <p class="muted">The strongest test result in each area and year, from 0 (nothing unusual) to 1 (strongest). Darker cells are stronger; a column of dark cells is a bad year, a row of them a recurring problem.</p>
  <table class="yeargrid"><thead><tr><th>Accounting area</th>{% for p in m.periods %}<th class="num">{{ p }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr></thead>
  <tbody>{% for a in m.areas %}<tr><td>{{ a.area }}</td>{% for c in a["values"] %}<td class="cell l{{ c.level }}" title="{{ a.area }}, {{ m.periods[loop.index0] }}: {{ c.v }}">{{ "%.2f"|format(c.v) if c.v >= 0.01 else '' }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table>
</div>
<div class="card">{% if m.charts.earnings_cash %}{{ m.charts.earnings_cash|safe }}{% else %}<h3>Net income vs cash from operations</h3><p>Not shown: for this type of company, operating cash flow does not measure how much of its profit turns into cash.</p>{% endif %}<p class="muted">Over time, profits should turn into cash. A persistent gap between net income and the cash the business generates is the most common sign that profits rely heavily on estimates.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Pressures on management</h3><p class="muted">These are not warning signs in themselves, but pressure (financial strain, leadership changes) makes earnings management more likely.</p><ul class="tight">{% for p in m.pressure %}<li><strong>{{ p.name }} ({{ p.period }}):</strong> {{ p.rationale }}</li>{% else %}<li>{{ m.none_text }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></div>
</section>

<section id="findings">
<h2>Suspicious Accounting Anomalies</h2>
{% for f in m.findings %}
<article class="card finding" id="f-{{ f.rank }}">
  <h3>{{ f.rank }}. {{ f.title }}</h3>
  <div class="meta"><span>{{ f.years_text }}</span><span>Strength of evidence: {{ f.strength }} ({{ "%.2f"|format(f.score) }} of 1)</span><span>Based on: {{ f.tests|join('; ') }}</span>
    <span class="audit {{ f.audit.status if f.audit else 'unverified' }}">{{ '✓' if f.audit and f.audit.status != 'unverified' else '!' }} {{ f.audit_label }}</span></div>
  <div class="yearstrip" aria-label="Years flagged">{% for t in f.timeline %}<span class="{{ 'on' if t.flagged else '' }}" title="{{ t.period }}: {{ 'flagged' if t.flagged else 'not flagged' }}">{{ t.period|replace('FY', '') }}</span>{% endfor %}</div>
  <p><strong>What we found:</strong> {{ f.what_found }}</p>
  <p><strong>Why this is unusual:</strong> {{ f.why_unusual }}</p>
  <p><strong>What it could mean financially:</strong> {{ f.what_it_means }}</p>
  <p><strong>Investigation ({{ f.investigation_status }}):</strong> {{ f.investigation }}</p>
  <dl class="kv">
    <dt>Estimated effect on pre-tax profit (latest year flagged)</dt><dd>{{ f.impact_text }}{% if f.impact_basis %} <span class="muted">(how it was estimated: {{ f.impact_basis }})</span>{% endif %}</dd>
    <dt>Is it material?</dt><dd>{{ f.materiality_text }}</dd>
    <dt>Other reasons it could matter</dt><dd>{{ f.sab99_text }}</dd>
  </dl>
  {% if f.chart %}{{ f.chart|safe }}{% elif f.strength_chart %}{{ f.strength_chart|safe }}{% else %}<p class="muted">Trend chart: not applicable, because this test does not measure a ratio over time.</p>{% endif %}
  <details open><summary>What the tests found (newest first; {{ f.signals|length }} of {{ f.signals_total }} results)</summary>
    {% for s in f.signals %}<div class="card">
      <h3>{{ s.name }} <span class="muted">· severity {{ "%.2f"|format(s.severity) }} · {{ s.period or 'latest period' }}</span></h3>
      <p>{{ s.rationale }}</p>
      <p class="reading"><strong>What this result means:</strong> {{ s.reading }}</p>
      <dl class="kv"><dt>What the test checks</dt><dd>{{ s.what or m.none_text }}</dd><dt>Why it matters</dt><dd>{{ s.why or m.none_text }}</dd><dt>How to interpret it</dt><dd>{{ s.how_to_read or m.none_text }}</dd></dl>
    </div>{% endfor %}
  </details>
  <details><summary>Supporting evidence: reported figures ({{ f.figures|length }} of {{ f.figures_total }})</summary>
    {{ f.graph|safe }}
    <div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Figure</th><th>Source</th><th class="num">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    {% for e in f.figures %}<tr><td>{{ e.label }} <span class="muted">· {{ e.kind_label }}</span></td>
      <td>{% if e.doc_url %}<a href="{{ e.doc_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ e.source }}</a>{% else %}{{ e.source }}{% endif %}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ e.value_fmt or '' }}</td></tr>{% else %}<tr><td colspan="3">{{ m.none_text }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
    </tbody></table></div>
  </details>
  <details><summary>Supporting evidence: quotes from the filings ({{ f.quotes|length }} of {{ f.quotes_total }})</summary>
    {% for e in f.quotes %}<blockquote>“{{ e.quote }}” <span class="muted">— {{ e.label }},</span> {% if e.doc_url %}<a href="{{ e.doc_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ e.source }}</a>{% else %}{{ e.source }}{% endif %}</blockquote>{% else %}<p>{{ m.none_text }}</p>{% endfor %}
  </details>
  <details><summary>Independent re-check ({% if f.audit %}{{ f.audit.rounds|length }} round{{ 's' if f.audit.rounds|length != 1 }}{% else %}not run{% endif %})</summary>{% if f.audit %}
    <p class="muted">A separate check re-reads every figure and quote from the original filings and recalculates the impact. Problems are corrected and re-checked, up to three rounds.</p>
    <div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Round</th><th>Check</th><th>Result</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    {% for r in f.audit.rounds %}{% for c in r.checks %}<tr><td>{{ r.round }}</td><td>{{ c.label }}</td><td><span class="pill {{ 'flagged' if c.status == 'fail' else 'normal' }}">{{ {'pass': 'passed', 'fail': 'failed', 'warn': 'note'}.get(c.status, c.status) }}</span></td><td>{{ c.detail }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
    {% for fix in r.corrections %}<tr><td>{{ r.round }}</td><td>Correction</td><td><span class="pill normal">applied</span></td><td>{{ fix }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}{% endfor %}
    </tbody></table></div>{% else %}<p>This anomaly was not independently re-checked.</p>{% endif %}</details>
  <details><summary>Innocent explanations to rule out</summary><ul class="tight">{% for a in f.alternatives %}<li>{{ a }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></details>
  <details open><summary>Questions to ask management or the auditors</summary><ul class="tight">{% for q in f.questions %}<li>{{ q }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></details>
</article>
{% else %}<p>No accounting anomaly met the reporting threshold in any year.</p>
{% endfor %}
</section>

{% if m.set_aside %}<section id="setaside">
<h2>Results set aside as probable test errors</h2>
<p class="muted">{{ m.set_aside_note }}</p>
{% for s in m.set_aside %}<div class="card"><h3>{{ s.title }}{% if s.years %} <span class="muted">· {{ s.years }}</span>{% endif %}</h3><p class="muted">Based on: {{ s.tests|join('; ') }}</p><p><strong>Why it was set aside:</strong> {{ s.reason }}</p></div>{% endfor %}
</section>{% endif %}

<section id="tests">
<h2>All tests performed</h2>
<p class="muted">Every test ran separately for each year. Severity runs from 0 (nothing unusual) to 1 (strongest); a result is flagged at {{ "%.1f"|format(m.flag_at) }}. "Explained" means the result was unusual but a known legitimate cause was found. "Held back" means the result or one of its inputs was physically impossible (for example a part larger than its whole), so it was not counted.</p>
{% for y in m.tests %}
<details class="card"><summary><strong>{{ m.periods[loop.index0] }}</strong> - {{ y.flagged }} flagged · {{ y.statuses.ok }} tests ran, {{ y.statuses.skipped }} could not run, {{ y.statuses['n/a'] }} do not apply, {{ y.statuses.error }} failed</summary>
{% for fam in y.families %}
<h3>{{ fam.name }} <span class="muted">· {{ fam.flagged }} flagged of {{ fam.ran }} that ran</span></h3>
<div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Test</th><th>Result</th><th class="num">Severity</th><th class="num">Peer percentile</th><th>What was found</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for r in fam.rows %}<tr><td>{{ r.name }}{% if r.period %}<div class="muted">{{ r.period }}</div>{% endif %}</td><td><span class="pill {{ r.status|replace('/', '') }}">{{ r.status_label }}</span></td>
<td class="num">{{ "%.2f"|format(r.severity) if r.severity is not none else '' }}</td><td class="num">{{ r.pct_peer if r.pct_peer is not none else '' }}</td><td>{{ r.detail }}
{% if r.reading and r.reading != r.detail %}<div class="reading">{{ r.reading }}</div>{% endif %}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</tbody></table></div>
{% endfor %}
</details>
{% endfor %}
</section>

<section id="text">
<h2>Changes in the company's disclosures</h2>
{% for t in m.text_changes %}<div class="card"><h3>{{ t.name }} <span class="muted">· {{ t.period }}</span></h3><p>{{ t.rationale }}</p>{% for q in t.quotes %}<blockquote>{{ q.quote }} <a href="{{ q.doc_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ q.source }}</a></blockquote>{% endfor %}</div>{% else %}<p class="muted">The text review did not flag disclosure changes in any year.</p>{% endfor %}
</section>

<section id="method">
<h2>How this review works</h2>
<div class="card">
<dl class="kv">
  <dt>Company</dt><dd>{{ m.company.match_note }}</dd>
  <dt>Company type</dt><dd>{{ m.profile.label }}. {{ m.profile.description }}{% for n in m.profile.notes %} {{ n }}{% endfor %}</dd>
  <dt>What was analysed</dt><dd>{{ m.analysis_type }}. The figures come from the company's filings with the US Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC).</dd>
  <dt>Years</dt><dd>Each of the {{ m.years }} fiscal years was analysed on its own, with its own comparison group and the history available up to that year; findings were then matched across years. Each anomaly's estimated effect, investigation and re-check use the most recent year in which it was flagged.</dd>
  <dt>Point in time</dt><dd>Each year was analysed with the filings public by the end of its own filing season ({{ m.as_of }} for the last year) (SEC comment letters about each year's annual report, which come later, are the one exception), and each year's figures are taken as first reported, before any later corrections.</dd>
  <dt>Comparison group (latest year)</dt><dd>{{ m.peer_method }}</dd>
  <dt>Legitimate causes checked</dt><dd>{% if m.explain_conditions %}{{ m.explain_conditions|join('; ') }}{% else %}No acquisition, change in accounting standards or stock split was found in any year reviewed, so no results were discounted for those reasons.{% endif %}</dd>
  <dt>Data notes</dt><dd><ul class="tight">{% for n in m.notes %}<li>{{ n }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></dd>
</dl>
<details><summary>Comparison companies, latest year ({{ m.peers|length }})</summary><ul class="tight">{% for p in m.peers %}<li>{{ p.name }}</li>{% else %}<li>None: no comparable peer group could be formed.</li>{% endfor %}</ul></details>
<details><summary>Filings read ({{ m.documents|length }})</summary><ul class="tight">{% for d in m.documents %}<li><a href="{{ d.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ d.label }}</a></li>{% endfor %}</ul></details>
<p class="muted">Limitations: this review looks for unusual patterns in public filings. It cannot verify cash, assets or transactions, and segment-level figures are not used. The earliest years have less history to compare against, so some tests could not run in them.</p>
</div>
</section>

<section id="glossary">
<h2>Glossary</h2>
<div class="card"><dl class="glossary">{% for term, meaning in m.glossary %}<dt>{{ term }}</dt><dd>{{ meaning }}</dd>{% endfor %}</dl></div>
<p class="disclaimer">{{ m.disclaimer }}</p>
</section>
</main>
</body>
</html>
